{
  "about": "Lighting keyframes for the day/night cycle and the bleak-to-bloomed arc. The game interpolates by time of day around the cycle (dawn -> day -> dusk -> night -> dawn), then blends the two moods by light quality: bleak at 0, bloomed (solarpunk by day, lunarpunk by night) at 1. Light quality is local, a field of 10 m cells driven mostly by plant density; the global lights use the value sampled at the camera, and ground_tint and accents use each cell's own value. Colours are sRGB. Lux values are physical-ish illuminance for Bevy; exposure_ev100 is the camera exposure for that key. emissive_gain scales module and creature emission relative to its daytime appearance (applied after exposure compensation), so lights glow more at night and in the bloomed world. accents[0] is the modules' amber; the rest are flora colours. Authored by art (docs/art/style-guide.md); the cycle and the field are game logic.",
